{"results":[{"url":"https://m.facebook.com/TheIndianSun/videos/comedian-anirban-dasgupta-weighs-in-on-the-recent-controversy-surrounding-kunal-/1165456971370703/","final_url":"https://www.facebook.com/TheIndianSun/videos/comedian-anirban-dasgupta-weighs-in-on-the-recent-controversy-surrounding-kunal-/1165456971370703/?_rdr","title":"Comedian Anirban Dasgupta 🎤😂 weighs in on the recent controversy surrounding Kunal Kamra. Full interview dropping soon—stay tuned! ⏳🎬 \n\n#Comedy 🎭 #FreedomOfSpeech 🗣️ #AnirbanDasgupta #KunalKamra #KunalKamraControversy 🔥 #TheIndianSun | The Indian Sun","description":"Comedian Anirban Dasgupta 🎤😂 weighs in on the recent controversy surrounding Kunal Kamra. Full interview dropping soon—stay tuned! ⏳🎬 \n\n#Comedy 🎭 #FreedomOfSpeech 🗣️ #AnirbanDasgupta #KunalKamra...","language":"en","text":"1,082 Assisted Deaths in Queensland: Are Safeguards Enough?\nMore than 1,000 people died through voluntary assisted dying in Queensland in just one year. Now, questions are being raised about whether the safeguards are adequate.\nOfficial figures show 1,082 assisted deaths in 2025-26, an increase of 36% compared with the scheme's first full financial year. Assisted dying now accounts for approximately 3% of all deaths in Queensland.\nThe figures have prompted Right To Life, an organisation opposed to assisted dying, to call for an independent inquiry.\nConcerns include access to palliative care, transparency around complications and proposals to allow greater use of telehealth and reconsider eligibility for people with dementia.\nVoluntary assisted dying is now operating in all six Australian states and the ACT, making the debate relevant well beyond Queensland.\nBut rising numbers alone do not establish that safeguards are failing.\nThe central question remains: How should Australia balance an individual's right to choose how they die with the need to protect vulnerable people?\n🎥 Watch our report and share your views.\n📰 Read the full story:\nhttps://www.theindiansun.com.au/2026/11/03/queensland-assisted-dying-figures-prompt-calls-for-independent-inquiry/\n#Queensland #AssistedDying #VoluntaryAssistedDying #Healthcare #PalliativeCare","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":11387.42865799577,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}